# L §5.16: "An ask line's own projection is no decision: it reads an amount after t by its random clause, by the
# line's query, or on a path by that path's sample"; with none of them it is refused (L §8.3 LOAD-RANDOM
# `<projection> reaches random <x> after <t> with no random clause or query`). The reality of
# L5_16_projection_random, its projection without a clause, no query and no path. (Writer 8: the same line on a path
# reads the samples, L5_16_ask_projection_path.)
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind spends: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input spend_mu: money PLN
input spend_sd: money PLN
input spend_dom: int
def spend[m in months]: dist PLN = normal(spend_mu, spend_sd) to 1e-9 at end_of(m)

move buy[m in months]: spends
  on day_of(m, spend_dom)
  at end_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round(spend[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  spend_mu = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  spend_sd = 100.00 PLN "own"
  spend_dom = 15 "own"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask r4: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM ask r4: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01 is random; apply a query (m.tally:32)
